    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338017/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday, Feb. 21, 1908
Warm Fine.
Fra Filippo. 
Worked. Went to Schumann concert and did not enjoy it much. though  music always sets one’s brain going. Alberto confessed the Dichterlieder were “not very musical”.
Had tea with Placci. He quoted one of Mrs. Moore’s famous balivernes, her description of the ceremony where the Pope washed the feet of the poor men, “J’ai vu le Pope qui avec une grande pompe a donné un lavement à douze pauvres prêtres.”
Tired. One does get  so  tired. This winter I feel I am growing old. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 74 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

